  "title": "The Great Depression (from the Wall Street crash of 1929)",
  "summary": "The stock market crash of October 1929, centred on the New York Stock Exchange, ended the prosperity of the 1920s. The Dow fell nearly 13 percent on 28 October and nearly 12 percent the next day, and kept sliding until the summer of 1932. A worldwide depression followed, with over a quarter of the American workforce jobless at its depths.",
